# OintOS Bootloader Packages
#
# Workaround for Ubuntu live-build Bug 2154055: lb_binary_grub tries to
# install the obsolete 'grub-legacy' package, which no longer exists in
# Ubuntu 26.04 ("E: Package 'grub-legacy' has no installation candidate").
#
# Pre-installing the correct modern GRUB packages into the chroot lets
# live-build's grub binary step succeed instead of reaching for grub-legacy.
#
# IMPORTANT conflicts to avoid:
#   - grub-pc and grub-efi-amd64 CONFLICT (both provide grub-install).
#     Do NOT install both full packages.
#   - The *-bin (modules) packages do NOT conflict and provide the GRUB
#     binaries/modules for the respective firmware.
#
# Selection for the OintOS hybrid (BIOS+EFI) ISO:
#   - grub-pc            : BIOS GRUB 2 (the canonical grub-install provider)
#   - grub-efi-amd64-bin : EFI GRUB modules (files, no conflicting install)
#   - grub-pc-bin        : BIOS GRUB modules
#   - grub2-common/grub-common : shared scaffolding
#
# (grub-efi-amd64 full package is intentionally NOT installed: it conflicts
#  with grub-pc and would re-poison the whole apt transaction.)

grub2-common
grub-common
grub-pc
grub-pc-bin
grub-efi-amd64-bin